---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="How GICT handles refunds, cancellations and batch transfers for its training programmes, including the timelines and conditions that apply."
  active="/refund-policy"
>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 21 October 2026</p>
  <p>
    This page explains the general approach to refunds and cancellations. The specific terms for your
    enrolment are stated in your admission offer, fee receipt and any signed agreement. If there is a
    conflict, those documents prevail.
  </p>

  <h2>Before you pay</h2>
  <p>
    Ask admissions for the current fee schedule, the cohort dates and the cancellation terms in writing.
    Do not rely on an old page, a social-media post or an informal message for the fee and refund position.
  </p>

  <h2>If you cancel</h2>
  <p>
    A cancellation request should be sent in writing to <a href="mailto:admissions@gict.edu.pk">admissions@gict.edu.pk</a>.
    The amount refundable, if any, depends on the date of the request, the cost already incurred and the
    terms in your admission documents. Application or administrative charges may be non-refundable where
    the admission documents say so.
  </p>

  <h2>If GICT cancels or reschedules</h2>
  <p>
    If GICT cancels a cohort, you may choose a full refund of the programme fee paid or a transfer to another
    available cohort. If a cohort is rescheduled, we will contact you with the new dates and the options
    available.
  </p>

  <h2>After the programme starts</h2>
  <p>
    Refunds after a programme has started are generally not available, except where required by law or
    expressly agreed in writing. Missed sessions are not normally refunded. Recordings, where offered, are
    subject to the programme terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Batch transfer</h2>
  <p>
    A transfer to another cohort may be available before the programme starts, subject to seat availability
    and any fee difference. Transfers are not guaranteed and must be confirmed in writing by admissions.
  </p>

  <h2>How refunds are processed</h2>
  <p>
    Approved refunds are returned through the original payment method where possible. Processing time depends
    on the bank or payment provider. GICT may ask for identification and payment evidence to prevent fraud.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Contact admissions on <a href="tel:+92518442474">051 8442474</a> or
    <a href="mailto:admissions@gict.edu.pk">admissions@gict.edu.pk</a> before paying if anything is unclear.
  </p>

  <div class="prose-note">
    This page describes a general process and is not a substitute for the specific terms in your admission
    offer. GICT should confirm the final policy with its management and legal adviser.
  </div>
</LegalLayout>
